+# UC19 Update Record Design
+
+Purpose: implement issue20/FR-RC-04 for an owner or current read/write recipient replacing one existing encrypted record with optimistic revision checking. This is architectural work: new Domain/Data/Command/HTTP interfaces and the first cross-owner content writer. Existing all-issues authorization replaces repeated design/plan/transition approvals. Independent security and actual-client approvals remain development-only deferred; release gates unchanged.
+
+Sources: fresh UC19 main/allfiveAF; common entity/record/folder/association/grant fields and authorization matrix; BR08/09/27; workflow/testing/technology/operations; existing profile online update, record get/list/create, profile associations and protection rotation. No plaintext, key material, migration or dependency change. Preserve the primary user checkout. Start isolated feature/uc-19-update-record only after UC18 verified integration DoD.
+
+## Approaches
+
+1. Reuse owner-only ProfileUpdateStore logic with a shared flag: reject because permission, ancestry and cross-owner lock order differ.
+2. Read permission using get then update separately: reject because revocation, hierarchy and native evidence can become stale.
+3. Targeted transactional authority snapshot, ordered resource locks, reload, and a guarded write: prefer; preserves native/current scope, one winner and no foreign account/profile locks. Extra bounded target-owner collection locking and SQL complexity buy a clear lock order. Complete ancestry is reevaluated inside the final write statement, without folder locks that would conflict with existing creation lock order. No general permission framework/refactor is needed.
+
+## Public contract
+
+PUT /api/records/{id}, canonical lowercase nonzero D UUID, current Heimdall identity and one canonical X-Cerberus-Vault-Access handle. Strict UTF8 JSON/no BOM/compression/duplicate/unknown/case/numericstrings, no query. Exactly required expectedRevision, envelope, editedAt. No recordId/ownerId/profileIds/folderId/collectionIds/key wrappers in body. Native cerberus-content-v1 with safe positive epoch and canonical binary fields. ExpectedRevision safe positive; UTC editedAt >=10ticks, floor to microseconds before binding, including pre2000. Same epoch only; same envelope allowed, changed envelope requires fresh salt AND nonce. Content-key rotation remains protection flow. Matching revision accepts older/equal/new edit time; UC49 offline LWW is separate.
+
+Success200 record_updated with exactly recordId/revision/serverSequence/editedAt. No ciphertext, relationship graph, owner/internal/grant/pin/credential fields. Current immutable owner/parent/memberships/profiles stay unchanged; no structural parent revision changes for content-only update. Record revision advances exactly once, new greater safe global serverSequence/concurrency stamp, normalized client editedAt. Lost-success retry with old revision409 preserves winner. All responses no-store; common oversized request413 empty.
+
+## Current scope and errors
+
+Actor active/nonterminal; current session hashed verifier, positive matching policy/generation, issued<=statement time, exclusive expiry or explicitly disabled renewal with null expiry, current owned active/nonterminal selection. Missing/invalid identity or missing handle401; invalid syntax400; missing/closing/terminal actor404; current invalid session/selection403.
+
+Current record scope matches UC18: accountwide own, selected own direct ProfileRecord or ProfileFolder ancestor, eligible owned/shared CollectionRecord or CollectionFolder ancestor, selected restricted to ProfileCollection links. Complete same-owner active ancestry, visited cycle termination, even direct admission. Hidden target/owner/ancestor/unselected/revoked collection/grant404 before native corruption or revision conflict; relevant fully active cycle503. Native foreign contributing grants (RO/RW) bind current collection epoch/envelope, exact grant ID/revision, immutable owner author pin and recipient identity/key pin. Invalid relevant native evidence503 whole transaction. A valid visible record with only RO permission403 before revision conflict; own or at least one valid current included RW grant permits content write. No create/delete/relationship rights conferred.
+
+Validate only target metadata/envelope; unrelated records/order/native data cannot fail this operation. Strict stored native JSON handles quoted numbers, duplicate/unknown/case shapes. Safe positive target revision/sequence and UTC storage time mandatory. Expected mismatch or revision/sequence exhaustion409; corrupt stored metadata503; changed epoch/reused salt or nonce400. Dependency outage/timeout503 rollback; caller cancellation propagates. Every failure has no content mutation or partial output.
+
+## Transaction and races
+
+Own actor account NO KEY UPDATE -> own session UPDATE -> own selected profile UPDATE (when any) -> current eligible target-owner collections SHARE sorted publicGUID -> current recipient grants SHARE sorted publicGUID -> target record NO KEY UPDATE. No foreign account/profile/protection locks. Future sharing/membership writers must honor collection->grant before affected content locks, never recipient account/profile afterward. No folder row locks: existing RecordCreateStore locks leaf-to-root folders, so adding publicGUID-ordered ancestor locks here could deadlock with concurrent creation. Initial structural permission is resolved for only one potential record before resource locks; hidden target does not lock/inspect arbitrary foreign inventory.
+
+After waits reload current authority, target scope, complete ancestry and native evidence in one targeted SQL snapshot. Require every final contributing collection/grant to be among held validated locks; new unlocked authority rows409 reload instead of acquiring an earlier lock late. Complete ancestry/visibility is recomputed inside the final guarded UPDATE so a committed move or trash is judged at that statement, including newly visited ancestors; no stale captured folder path is trusted. Reloaded hidden scopes404 and expired authority403 take precedence. Revalidate target revision after lock; competing own/recipient writers have one winner. Final guarded UPDATE uses statement_timestamp and current actor/session/selection/owner/resource/complete recursive ancestry/collection/grant lifecycle and only validated held write routes. It cannot admit new unvalidated permissions. Zero rows classified with fresh authority/scope then safe conflict; any unexpected postwrite metadata/sequence or provider failure rolls back.
+
+Protection rotation locks owner account/session, reads record/folder inventory without row locks, then collections UPDATE and grants UPDATE in publicGUID order, followed by optimistic stamped writes. UC19 shares that collection->grant order and does not lock owner account, avoiding reciprocal account cycles. If recipient wins after rotation read, rotation's optimistic content stamp rejects stale replacement; if rotation wins, expected revision/epoch validation rejects stale recipient update. Public RecipientKey and AuthorKey are immutable under current rotation contract; no private key/decryption involved. Concurrent lifecycle can linearize before or after update; final statement denies already committed closure/terminal state.
+
+## Interfaces and components
+
+Domain/Records/RecordUpdateContracts.cs: strict JsonRequired RecordUpdateInput(long ExpectedRevision,EncryptedEnvelope Envelope,DateTimeOffset EditedAt), IsValid(); RecordUpdateRequest(Guid Actor,string AccessVerifier,Guid RecordId,RecordUpdateInput Input); IRecordUpdateStore.UpdateAsync(request,ct)->VaultResult<RecordCreateDetails> (reuse four-field metadata).
+Data/Records/RecordUpdateStore.cs: purpose-built transaction/targeted internal snapshots/ordered locks/native evidence and final guarded mutation; reuse CollectionGrantBinding. No public permission graph or general abstraction. Command/Records/UpdateRecordCommand,UpdateRecordValidator,UpdateRecordHandler,UpdateRecordOutput,RecordUpdateMessages: immutable server context; strict pre-store context/input/hash; safe allowlist; null/error-with-data/unknown/mismatched output503. Output expected next revision/normalized time/safe sequence; cancellation. RecordsController PUT + VaultProofBody + DI/status annotations, no route ambiguity.
+
+## Flow mapping and verification
+
+Main: Data owned+sharedRW selected/accountwide direct/descendant/overlap and metadata/ciphertext/no relation mutation; Command strict forwarding/result; actual HTTP native Master/PerProfile handles and current native shared grants.
+AF01: domain+validator+HTTP canonical route/header/body/envelope/epoch/salt/nonce/time failures400 and no writes.
+AF02: Data+HTTP absent/foreign/unselected/trash/terminal/hidden ancestor/owner/grant404 before malformed evidence/conflict, current link removal/descendant moves.
+AF03: identity401/provideroutage503; missing/bad/expired/revoked/policy/generation/selection403; RO403 vs hidden404; no mutation, no foreign graph.
+AF04: owner+two recipients concurrent expected revisions exactly one winner, lost-response retry409, rotation/content race, new unheld collection/grant authority409, exhaustion409; compare winning cipher/state.
+AF05: outage503, injected afterwrite failure rollback/retry, sequence regression503 rollback, caller cancellation propagated.
+
+Additional tests: expiry during every account/session/profile/collection/grant/record wait and immediatelybeforeUPDATE; grantrevocation/accessdowngrade/memberremove/folderreparent whileblocked; concurrent record creation under the same parent without deadlock; terminal introduced at guardedUPDATE; malformed relevant native signature/epoch/revision/identity/pins/JSON vs irrelevant hidden grants; actual SQL target candidate<=1/no inventory traversal; reciprocal sharedwrites no deadlock and no foreign account/profile locks.
+
+Named whole Data/Command/Web suites; full fresh unfiltered sixfamilies >=90%line/zero fail/skip/reportbranch; native audit/corpus/helpers, lockedrestore/NuGet, OpenAPI actual body/4fields/status audit, spec/helper/diff. One fresh wholebranch review and one blocking TDD fixpass, exhaustive rulings/costs/minors. Fresh exact-head branch-policy/test/dockerSUCCESS+MERGEABLE/CLEAN+unchanged tested develop before normal matchheadsquash; complete issue20/project/9DoD/remoteabsence/developtestedtree/primarySHA/archive then UC20. Global terminal-GUID collision remains conservative and must be repaired before ANYphysicalpurge; never null a selected profile onpurge. Known shared OpenAPI required/header/non-null/empty413 minors stay tracked before release.
